module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Module.OppositeOfCommSemiring
public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Geometric.RingsTangentSpaceIdentification

/-!
# Realizing a square-zero extension of `P` by a first-order flat deformation

Let `k` be a field, `P` a `k`-algebra, `V` a `k`-vector space and `k ⊕ V` the square-zero
extension of `k` by `V` of Stacks 06IB. `StacksFrontier/Deformation/Examples/Geometric/`
`RingsTangentSpaceIdentification.lean` turns a first-order flat deformation of `P` over
`k ⊕ V` into a square-zero extension of the `k`-algebra `P` by the `P`-module `P ⊗[k] V`,
which is the shape in which Stacks 0GPT classifies it by `Ext¹_P(NL_{P/k}, P ⊗[k] V)`.

This file goes the other way, which is the surjectivity half of the tangent-space clause of
Stacks 0DY3: an *arbitrary* square-zero extension `E` of `P` by `P ⊗[k] V` carries a
`k ⊕ V`-algebra structure on its middle ring, for which it *is* a first-order flat deformation
of `P`, and the extension that deformation determines is `E` again.

The structural map is forced: `k ⊕ V → E.B'` must send `(c, v)` to
`algebraMap k E.B' c + ι (1 ⊗ v)` for `ι : P ⊗[k] V → E.B'` the identification of the kernel,
because the action of the augmentation ideal on the kernel is multiplication through the
reduction. Flatness is then the only thing to prove, and it comes from **Stacks 063Y** in the
form `Ideal.bijective_tensorSMulHomToKer_iff`: the canonical map
`I ⊗[k ⊕ V] E.B' → ker(E.B' → P)` for `I` the augmentation ideal is bijective because
`p ⊗ v ↦ inr v ⊗ s p`, for a `k`-linear section `s` of the reduction, is a two-sided inverse of
the comparison `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] E.B' → P ⊗[k] V` through which it factors.

## Main definitions

* `Deformation.Examples.toRed` and `Deformation.Examples.kerIncl`: the reduction and the
  kernel inclusion of a square-zero extension of `P` by `P ⊗[k] V`, with their source and
  target spelled `P` and `P ⊗[k] V` rather than through the projections of the extension
  problem of Stacks 0GPT.
* `Deformation.Examples.realizationHom` and `Deformation.Examples.realizationAlgebra`: the
  structural map `k ⊕ V → E.B'` and the `k ⊕ V`-algebra structure it defines.
* `Deformation.Examples.realizationTensorSection`: the inverse `P ⊗[k] V → I ⊗[k ⊕ V] E.B'`
  of the comparison map of Stacks 063Y, built from a `k`-linear section of the reduction.
* `Deformation.Examples.isoRealization` and `Deformation.Examples.isoRealizationOfEq`: the
  isomorphism of square-zero extensions between the extension the realized deformation
  determines and `E` itself.

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.isFirstOrderReduction_toRed`,
  `Deformation.Examples.kerCondition_toRed`: the reduction of the realized deformation is
  compatible with the augmentation and its kernel is the ideal generated by the augmentation
  ideal.
* `Deformation.Examples.isScalarTower_realization` and
  `Deformation.Examples.algebraMap_eq_realizationHom_inl`: the realizing structural map sends
  `inl c` to the structural map of `E` over `k`, so the tower condition over `k` is a
  consequence of the hypothesis `hstr` and never has to be assumed, for the structure `E`
  carries or for any other one.
* `Deformation.Examples.flat_realization`: **the realized deformation is flat over `k ⊕ V`**,
  by Stacks 063Y.
* `Deformation.Examples.isPushout_realization`: `P` is the base change of the realized
  deformation along the augmentation `k ⊕ V → k`, which is the cartesian square an object of
  the deformation category of Stacks 0DY1 carries.
* `Deformation.Examples.extClass_firstOrderExtension_realization` and
  `Deformation.Examples.extClass_firstOrderExtension_eq`: the class in
  `Ext¹_P(NL_{P/k}, P ⊗[k] V)` of the extension determined by the realized deformation is the
  class of `E`. The second is the form a deformation-category datum delivers, where the
  reduction is only extensionally the reduction of `E`.
* `Deformation.Examples.isPushout_commRingCat_realization`: the cartesian square in
  `CommRingCat`, which is the shape a morphism of the category of flat algebras of Stacks 0DY1
  carries.

## Implementation notes

Nothing here carries the tag of Stacks 0DY3: this file supplies the surjectivity half of the
tangent-space clause as commutative algebra, and the clause itself is not yet assembled; the
deformation-category side of the surjectivity is
`StacksFrontier/Deformation/Examples/Geometric/RingsTangentSpaceEquivSurjective.lean` and the
injectivity side is `Deformation.Examples.tangentExtClass_injective` of
`StacksFrontier/Deformation/Examples/Geometric/RingsTangentSpaceInjection.lean`. The
infinitesimal-automorphism clause of that tag is
`Deformation.Examples.exists_infinitesimalAutomorphismGroupMulEquivDerivation` of
`StacksFrontier/Deformation/Examples/Geometric/RingsInfinitesimalAutomorphisms.lean`.

The `k ⊕ V`-algebra structure on `E.B'` is `Deformation.Examples.realizationAlgebra`, but the
lemmas about it are stated for an *arbitrary* `k ⊕ V`-algebra structure on `E.B'` whose
structural map is `Deformation.Examples.realizationHom`, recorded as the hypothesis `hstr`.
That keeps every statement free of a `letI` prefix; the instance is supplied, and `hstr`
discharged by `rfl`, only in the results that mention
`Deformation.Examples.firstOrderExtension`, which needs the instance to be stated at all.

The results about `Deformation.Examples.firstOrderExtension` are stated for an arbitrary
reduction `π` which agrees with `Deformation.Examples.toRed` extensionally, rather than for
`Deformation.Examples.toRed` itself, because an object of the deformation category of
Stacks 0DY1 presents its reduction through its own base-change square and so delivers it only
in that form.

For the same reason those results — the section `RealizedBase` — are also parametric in the
`k`-algebra structure on `E.B'`, which the section takes as a variable instead of using the one
`E` carries. A point of the deformation category presents its flat algebra as a `k`-algebra by
*transporting* the structure from its base through the presentation of that base as `k ⊕ V`, so
the structure it supplies has structural map `c ↦ algebraMap k E.B' c + kerIncl E (1 ⊗ₜ 0)`:
equal to the structural map of `E` but not definitionally so. Asking the elaborator to identify
the two is not merely slow but hopeless — it unfolds the identification of the kernel of `E` and
does not terminate within any heartbeat budget — whereas `hstr` pins the variable structure down
by `Deformation.Examples.algebraMap_eq_realizationHom_inl`, and
`Deformation.Examples.isoRealizationOfEq` compares the two structures by the identity of the
ring read as an isomorphism of `k`-algebras. `Deformation.Examples.flat_realization` omits the
tower condition for the same purpose: it is quoted in a context carrying that other structure,
where the tower condition over `k` holds for the other one instead.

`Deformation.Examples.tmul_eq_zero_of_mem_kerIdeal_smul` is a re-proof of
`Ideal.tmul_eq_zero_of_mem_smul_top` of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/GradedAlgebra/LiftPresentation.lean`, repeated here rather than
importing a graded-algebra file into a deformation-theory one; the same lemma is also
`private` in `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Flat/SquareZeroBaseChange.lean`.

The comparison `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] E.B' → P ⊗[k] V` itself is `conormalCompare`, which is `private`
in `StacksFrontier/Deformation/Examples/RingsTangentSpace.lean`; only its inverse is needed
here, so it is not re-proved. The inverse is built from
`Deformation.Examples.reductionSection`, a `k`-linear section of the reduction, so no
set-theoretic choice of lifts enters and no datum is extracted from an existence statement.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DY3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DY3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GPT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GPT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 063Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06IB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06IB)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe w

open CategoryTheory TensorProduct TrivSqZeroExt Stacks.Deformation

namespace Deformation.Examples

section Realization

variable {k : Type w} [Field k] {V : Type w} [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V]

/-- The right `k`-action on `V` agreeing with the left one, needed to form `k ⊕ V`. -/
local instance moduleMulOppositeRealization : Module kᵐᵒᵖ V :=
  Module.oppositeOfCommSemiring k V

/-- The two `k`-actions on `V` agree. -/
local instance isCentralScalarRealization : IsCentralScalar k V :=
  Module.isCentralScalar_oppositeOfCommSemiring k V

variable {P : Type w} [CommRing P] [Algebra k P]

/-- The augmentation `k ⊕ V → k` as an algebra structure on `k`. -/
local instance algebraTrivSqZeroExtBase : Algebra (TrivSqZeroExt k V) k :=
  (fstHom k k V).toRingHom.toAlgebra

/-- The `k`-algebra `P` as an algebra over `k ⊕ V`, through the augmentation. -/
local instance algebraTrivSqZeroExtTarget : Algebra (TrivSqZeroExt k V) P :=
  ((algebraMap k P).comp (fstHom k k V).toRingHom).toAlgebra

/-- The augmentation, the structural map of `P` and the composite form a tower. -/
local instance isScalarTowerTrivSqZeroExtBase : IsScalarTower (TrivSqZeroExt k V) k P :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- **The augmentation presents `k` as the quotient by the augmentation ideal.** -/
public def quotKerIdealAlgEquiv (k : Type w) [Field k] (V : Type w) [AddCommGroup V]
    [Module k V] [Module kᵐᵒᵖ V] [IsCentralScalar k V] :
    (TrivSqZeroExt k V ⧸ kerIdeal k V) ≃ₐ[k] k :=
  Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective (f := fstHom k k V)
    fun c ↦ ⟨inl c, fst_inl V c⟩

public lemma quotKerIdealAlgEquiv_mk (a : TrivSqZeroExt k V) :
    quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V (Ideal.Quotient.mk (kerIdeal k V) a) = a.fst := rfl

/-- The residue field of the augmentation ideal acts on `k` through the identification with
`k`. -/
local instance algebraQuotBase : Algebra (TrivSqZeroExt k V ⧸ kerIdeal k V) k :=
  (quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V).toRingEquiv.toRingHom.toAlgebra

/-- The residue field of the augmentation ideal acts on `P` through the identification with
`k`. -/
local instance algebraQuotTarget : Algebra (TrivSqZeroExt k V ⧸ kerIdeal k V) P :=
  ((algebraMap k P).comp (quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V).toRingEquiv.toRingHom).toAlgebra

local instance isScalarTowerQuotBase : IsScalarTower (TrivSqZeroExt k V ⧸ kerIdeal k V) k P :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun _ ↦ rfl

local instance isScalarTowerQuot :
    IsScalarTower (TrivSqZeroExt k V) (TrivSqZeroExt k V ⧸ kerIdeal k V) P :=
  ⟨fun x y z ↦ by
    induction y using Quotient.inductionOn' with
    | h a =>
        change algebraMap k P ((x * a).fst) * z
          = algebraMap k P x.fst * (algebraMap k P a.fst * z)
        rw [fst_mul, map_mul, mul_assoc]⟩

/-- `k` is flat over the residue field of the augmentation ideal: the identification of that
residue field with `k` is a linear equivalence onto the ring itself. -/
public lemma flat_quotKerIdeal_base :
    Module.Flat (TrivSqZeroExt k V ⧸ kerIdeal k V) k :=
  Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (M := TrivSqZeroExt k V ⧸ kerIdeal k V) (N := k)
    { toFun := (quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V).symm
      map_add' := map_add _
      map_smul' := fun r x ↦ by
        change (quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V).symm (quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V r * x)
          = r * (quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V).symm x
        rw [map_mul, AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
      invFun := quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V
      left_inv := (quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V).apply_symm_apply
      right_inv := (quotKerIdealAlgEquiv k V).symm_apply_apply }

/-- `P` is flat over the residue field of the augmentation ideal, that field being `k`. -/
public lemma flat_quotKerIdeal_target :
    Module.Flat (TrivSqZeroExt k V ⧸ kerIdeal k V) P :=
  haveI := flat_quotKerIdeal_base (k := k) (V := V)
  Module.Flat.trans (TrivSqZeroExt k V ⧸ kerIdeal k V) k P

variable (E : (algebraExtensionProblem k P (P ⊗[k] V)).CompatibleExtension.{w})

/-- The reduction of a square-zero extension of `P` by `P ⊗[k] V`, with its target spelled
`P`. -/
public def toRed : E.B' →ₐ[k] P := E.toB

/-- The identification of the kernel of a square-zero extension of `P` by `P ⊗[k] V` with
`P ⊗[k] V`, read as a map into the middle ring. -/
public def kerIncl : (P ⊗[k] V) →+ E.B' := kernelInclusion E

@[simp]
public lemma toRed_kerIncl (x : P ⊗[k] V) : toRed E (kerIncl E x) = 0 :=
  toB_kernelInclusion E x

public lemma kerIncl_mul_kerIncl (x y : P ⊗[k] V) : kerIncl E x * kerIncl E y = 0 :=
  kernelInclusion_mul_kernelInclusion E x y

public lemma mul_kerIncl (z : E.B') (x : P ⊗[k] V) :
    z * kerIncl E x = kerIncl E (toRed E z • x) :=
  mul_kernelInclusion E z x

public lemma kerIncl_injective : Function.Injective (kerIncl E) :=
  kernelInclusion_injective E

public lemma exists_eq_kerIncl {z : E.B'} (hz : toRed E z = 0) : ∃ x, kerIncl E x = z :=
  exists_eq_kernelInclusion E hz

public lemma toRed_surjective : Function.Surjective (toRed E) := E.surjective

public lemma ker_toRed_sq : RingHom.ker (toRed E).toRingHom ^ 2 = ⊥ := E.sq_zero

public lemma algebraMap_mul_kerIncl (c : k) (x : P ⊗[k] V) :
    algebraMap k E.B' c * kerIncl E x = kerIncl E (c • x) := by
  rw [mul_kerIncl]
  congr 1
  rw [AlgHom.commutes]
  exact algebraMap_smul P c x

/-- **The structural map of the first-order deformation realizing a square-zero extension.**
It sends `(c, v)` to `algebraMap k E.B' c + ι (1 ⊗ v)`, for `ι` the identification of the
kernel of `E` with `P ⊗[k] V`; the kernel being square zero makes this multiplicative. -/
public def realizationHom : TrivSqZeroExt k V →+* E.B' where
  toFun a := algebraMap k E.B' a.fst + kerIncl E ((1 : P) ⊗ₜ[k] a.snd)
  map_one' := by simp
  map_zero' := by simp
  map_add' a b := by
    simp only [fst_add, snd_add, map_add, TensorProduct.tmul_add]
    ring
  map_mul' a b := by
    simp only [fst_mul, snd_mul, map_mul, op_smul_eq_smul, TensorProduct.tmul_add,
      TensorProduct.tmul_smul, map_add]
    rw [← algebraMap_mul_kerIncl, ← algebraMap_mul_kerIncl]
    have h0 : kerIncl E ((1 : P) ⊗ₜ[k] b.snd) * kerIncl E ((1 : P) ⊗ₜ[k] a.snd) = 0 :=
      kerIncl_mul_kerIncl E _ _
    ring_nf
    rw [h0, add_zero]

public lemma realizationHom_apply (a : TrivSqZeroExt k V) :
    realizationHom E a = algebraMap k E.B' a.fst + kerIncl E ((1 : P) ⊗ₜ[k] a.snd) := rfl

public lemma realizationHom_inl (c : k) :
    realizationHom E (inl c) = algebraMap k E.B' c := by
  simp [realizationHom_apply]

public lemma realizationHom_inr (v : V) :
    realizationHom E (inr v) = kerIncl E ((1 : P) ⊗ₜ[k] v) := by
  simp [realizationHom_apply]

/-- **The `k ⊕ V`-algebra structure realizing a square-zero extension of `P` by `P ⊗[k] V`.**
-/
@[instance_reducible]
public def realizationAlgebra : Algebra (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' :=
  (realizationHom E).toAlgebra

public lemma realizationAlgebra_algebraMap (a : TrivSqZeroExt k V) :
    letI := realizationAlgebra E
    algebraMap (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' a = realizationHom E a := rfl

public lemma realizationIsScalarTower :
    letI := realizationAlgebra E
    IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' :=
  letI := realizationAlgebra E
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun c ↦ by
    rw [realizationAlgebra_algebraMap, algebraMap_eq_inl, realizationHom_inl]

/-! ### The realized deformation

Everything below is stated for an arbitrary `k ⊕ V`-algebra structure on the middle ring of
`E` whose structural map is `Deformation.Examples.realizationHom`; the hypothesis `hstr` says
exactly that, and `Deformation.Examples.realizationAlgebra` satisfies it by `rfl`. -/

section Realized

variable [Algebra (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B']
  (hstr : ∀ a : TrivSqZeroExt k V,
    algebraMap (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' a = realizationHom E a)

include hstr

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
/-- **The realizing structural map makes `k`, `k ⊕ V` and the middle ring of `E` a tower.**
The structural map carries `inl c` to the structural map of `E` as a `k`-algebra, so the tower
condition is a consequence of `hstr` and is never needed as a hypothesis. -/
public lemma isScalarTower_realization : IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun c ↦ by
    rw [algebraMap_eq_inl, hstr, realizationHom_inl]

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
/-- **The reduction of the realized deformation is compatible with the augmentation.** -/
public lemma isFirstOrderReduction_toRed : IsFirstOrderReduction V (toRed E) := by
  intro a
  rw [hstr, realizationHom_apply, map_add, toRed_kerIncl, add_zero, AlgHom.commutes]

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
/-- The augmentation ideal acts on the realized deformation by multiplying the reduction into
the identified kernel. -/
public lemma inr_smul_eq_kerIncl (v : V) (z : E.B') :
    (inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • z = kerIncl E (toRed E z ⊗ₜ[k] v) := by
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, hstr, realizationHom_inr, mul_comm, mul_kerIncl]
  congr 1
  rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul, mul_one]

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
/-- The identified kernel of `E` lies in the submodule generated by the augmentation ideal. -/
public lemma kerIncl_mem_kerIdeal_smul (y : P ⊗[k] V) :
    kerIncl E y ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B') := by
  induction y with
  | tmul p v =>
      obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := toRed_surjective E p
      have h : kerIncl E (p ⊗ₜ[k] v) = (inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • q := by
        rw [inr_smul_eq_kerIncl E hstr, hq]
      rw [h]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul ((mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl) Submodule.mem_top
  | add y y' hy hy' => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ hy hy'

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
/-- **The kernel of the reduction of the realized deformation is generated by the augmentation
ideal.** This is the hypothesis `hker` of `Deformation.Examples.firstOrderExtension`. -/
public lemma kerCondition_toRed (x : E.B') (hx : toRed E x = 0) :
    x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B') := by
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_kerIncl E hx
  exact kerIncl_mem_kerIdeal_smul E hstr y

/-- **The canonical map of the realized deformation is the identification of the kernel it
started from.** -/
public lemma firstOrderConormalHom_eq_kerIncl (x : P ⊗[k] V) :
    firstOrderConormalHom (V := V) (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) x = kerIncl E x := by
  induction x with
  | tmul p v =>
      obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := toRed_surjective E p
      rw [firstOrderConormalHom_tmul (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E)
        (kerCondition_toRed E hstr) p v q hq, inr_smul_eq_kerIncl E hstr, hq]
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy]

omit hstr

/-- A `k ⊕ V`-linear map vanishes on the submodule generated by the augmentation ideal as soon as
it kills every multiple of an element by an element of that ideal. -/
private theorem map_eq_zero_of_mem_kerIdeal_smul {M N : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [AddCommGroup N]
    [Module (TrivSqZeroExt k V) M] [Module (TrivSqZeroExt k V) N] (f : M →ₗ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] N)
    (hf : ∀ a ∈ kerIdeal k V, ∀ y, f (a • y) = 0) {z : M}
    (hz : z ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) M)) : f z = 0 :=
  Submodule.smul_induction_on hz (fun a ha y _ ↦ hf a ha y) fun u v hu hv ↦ by
    rw [map_add, hu, hv, add_zero]

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
/-- An elementary tensor over the augmentation ideal vanishes as soon as its second factor lies
in the submodule that ideal generates. This is a re-proof of
`Ideal.tmul_eq_zero_of_mem_smul_top` of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/GradedAlgebra/LiftPresentation.lean`. -/
private theorem tmul_eq_zero_of_mem_kerIdeal_smul (i : ↥(kerIdeal k V)) {z : E.B'}
    (hz : z ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B')) :
    (i ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] z : ↥(kerIdeal k V) ⊗[TrivSqZeroExt k V] E.B') = 0 := by
  refine map_eq_zero_of_mem_kerIdeal_smul (TensorProduct.mk _ _ _ i) (fun a ha y ↦ ?_) hz
  have hai : a • i = 0 := by
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    have h := Ideal.mul_mem_mul ha i.2
    rw [← pow_two, kerIdeal_sq] at h
    simpa using h
  rw [TensorProduct.mk_apply, ← TensorProduct.smul_tmul, hai, TensorProduct.zero_tmul]

/-- **The inverse of the comparison map of Stacks 063Y.** The additive map
`P ⊗[k] V → I ⊗[k ⊕ V] E.B'` carrying `p ⊗ v` to `inr v ⊗ s p`, for `s` the `k`-linear section
`Deformation.Examples.reductionSection` of the reduction. -/
public def realizationTensorSection :
    (P ⊗[k] V) →+ (↥(kerIdeal k V) ⊗[TrivSqZeroExt k V] E.B') :=
  TensorProduct.liftAddHom
    { toFun := fun p ↦
        { toFun := fun v ↦
            (⟨inr v, (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩ : ↥(kerIdeal k V))
              ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] reductionSection (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) p
          map_zero' := by
            rw [show (⟨inr (0 : V), (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩ : ↥(kerIdeal k V))
              = 0 from Subtype.ext (inr_zero k (M := V)), TensorProduct.zero_tmul]
          map_add' := fun v v' ↦ by
            rw [show (⟨inr (v + v'), (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩ : ↥(kerIdeal k V))
                = ⟨inr v, (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩
                  + ⟨inr v', (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩ from
              Subtype.ext (inr_add k v v'), TensorProduct.add_tmul] }
      map_zero' := by
        refine AddMonoidHom.ext fun v ↦ ?_
        change _ ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] reductionSection (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) 0 = 0
        rw [map_zero, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]
      map_add' := fun p p' ↦ by
        refine AddMonoidHom.ext fun v ↦ ?_
        change _ ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V]
          reductionSection (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) (p + p') = _
        rw [map_add, TensorProduct.tmul_add]
        rfl }
    fun c p v ↦ by
      change (⟨inr v, _⟩ : ↥(kerIdeal k V)) ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V]
          reductionSection (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) (c • p)
        = (⟨inr (c • v), _⟩ : ↥(kerIdeal k V)) ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V]
          reductionSection (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) p
      rw [show (⟨inr (c • v), (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩ : ↥(kerIdeal k V))
          = algebraMap k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) c • ⟨inr v, (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩ from
        Subtype.ext (by rw [algebraMap_eq_inl]; exact (inl_mul_inr c v).symm),
        TensorProduct.smul_tmul, map_smul]
      congr 1
      exact (algebraMap_smul (TrivSqZeroExt k V) c
        (reductionSection (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) p)).symm

public lemma realizationTensorSection_tmul (p : P) (v : V) :
    realizationTensorSection E (p ⊗ₜ[k] v)
      = (⟨inr v, (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩ : ↥(kerIdeal k V))
        ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] reductionSection (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) p := rfl

include hstr

/-- The comparison map of Stacks 063Y carries the section back to the identification of the
kernel. -/
public lemma tensorSMulHom_realizationTensorSection (x : P ⊗[k] V) :
    (kerIdeal k V).tensorSMulHom E.B' (realizationTensorSection E x) = kerIncl E x := by
  induction x with
  | tmul p v =>
      rw [realizationTensorSection_tmul, Ideal.tensorSMulHom_tmul]
      change (inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • _ = _
      rw [inr_smul_eq_kerIncl E hstr, apply_reductionSection]
  | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, hx, hy]

/-- The section is surjective: every elementary tensor `i ⊗ q` of `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] E.B'` is the
image of `π q ⊗ i.snd`, because two lifts of `π q` differ by an element of the submodule the
augmentation ideal generates and that ideal annihilates itself. -/
public lemma realizationTensorSection_surjective :
    Function.Surjective (realizationTensorSection E) := by
  intro z
  induction z with
  | tmul i q =>
      refine ⟨toRed E q ⊗ₜ[k] (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd, ?_⟩
      rw [realizationTensorSection_tmul]
      rw [show (⟨inr (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd, (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩ :
          ↥(kerIdeal k V)) = i from
        Subtype.ext ((mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V)).1 i.2).symm]
      have hmem : reductionSection (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) (toRed E q) - q
          ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B') := by
        refine kerCondition_toRed E hstr _ ?_
        rw [map_sub, apply_reductionSection, sub_self]
      have h0 : (i ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V]
          (reductionSection (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E) (toRed E q) - q) :
            ↥(kerIdeal k V) ⊗[TrivSqZeroExt k V] E.B') = 0 :=
        tmul_eq_zero_of_mem_kerIdeal_smul E i hmem
      rw [TensorProduct.tmul_sub, sub_eq_zero] at h0
      exact h0
  | add z z' hz hz' =>
      obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hz
      obtain ⟨x', hx'⟩ := hz'
      exact ⟨x + x', by rw [map_add, hx, hx']⟩

/-- **The comparison map of Stacks 063Y is injective for the realized deformation.** It
factors as the identification of the kernel composed with the surjective section, so its
injectivity is that of the identification. -/
public lemma injective_tensorSMulHom_realization :
    Function.Injective ((kerIdeal k V).tensorSMulHom E.B') := by
  intro z z' h
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := realizationTensorSection_surjective E hstr z
  obtain ⟨x', rfl⟩ := realizationTensorSection_surjective E hstr z'
  rw [tensorSMulHom_realizationTensorSection E hstr,
    tensorSMulHom_realizationTensorSection E hstr] at h
  rw [kerIncl_injective E h]

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
/-- **The realized deformation is flat over `k ⊕ V`**, which is the last hypothesis of
`Deformation.Examples.firstOrderExtension`.

This is **Stacks 063Y**: the canonical map `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] E.B' → ker(E.B' → P)` is bijective,
injectively by `Deformation.Examples.injective_tensorSMulHom_realization` and surjectively
because its image is the submodule generated by the augmentation ideal, which is that
kernel.

The tower condition is omitted rather than assumed: it follows from `hstr` by
`Deformation.Examples.isScalarTower_realization`, and leaving it out is what lets the
flatness be quoted in a context carrying a *different* `k`-algebra structure on `E.B'`. -/
public lemma flat_realization : Module.Flat (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' := by
  have := isScalarTower_realization E hstr
  let : Algebra E.B' P := (toRed E).toRingHom.toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' P :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun a ↦ (isFirstOrderReduction_toRed E hstr a).symm
  have := flat_quotKerIdeal_target (k := k) (V := V) (P := P)
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap E.B' P) := toRed_surjective E
  refine ((((kerIdeal k V).bijective_tensorSMulHomToKer_iff E.B' P (kerIdeal_sq k V) hsurj
    inferInstance).1 ⟨?_, ?_⟩).1)
  · intro z z' h
    exact injective_tensorSMulHom_realization E hstr (congrArg Subtype.val h)
  · intro y
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := exists_eq_kerIncl E (show toRed E (y : E.B') = 0 from y.2)
    exact ⟨realizationTensorSection E x,
      Subtype.ext ((tensorSMulHom_realizationTensorSection E hstr x).trans hx)⟩

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] hstr in
/-- Every element of `E.B' ⊗[k ⊕ V] k` is an elementary tensor `z ⊗ 1`: the augmentation
`k ⊕ V → k` is split by `inl`, so the second factor absorbs into the first. -/
private lemma exists_tmul_one (x : E.B' ⊗[TrivSqZeroExt k V] k) :
    ∃ z : E.B', z ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] (1 : k) = x := by
  induction x with
  | tmul z c =>
      refine ⟨(inl c : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • z, ?_⟩
      rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul]
      congr 1
      change (inl c : TrivSqZeroExt k V).fst * (1 : k) = c
      rw [fst_inl, mul_one]
  | add x y hx hy =>
      obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hx
      obtain ⟨z', rfl⟩ := hy
      exact ⟨z + z', TensorProduct.add_tmul _ _ _⟩

/-! ### The cartesian square -/

section Pushout

variable [Algebra E.B' P] [IsScalarTower (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' P]
  (hred : ∀ z : E.B', algebraMap E.B' P z = toRed E z)

include hred

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
/-- **`P` is the base change of the realized deformation along the augmentation `k ⊕ V → k`.**
This is the cartesian square which an object of the deformation category of Stacks 0DY1 over
the base `k ⊕ V` carries.

Both halves are elementary: `E.B' ⊗[k ⊕ V] k` is generated by the tensors `z ⊗ 1` because
`inl` splits the augmentation, the canonical map sends `z ⊗ 1` to the reduction of `z`, and the
reduction kills `z` exactly when `z` lies in the submodule the augmentation ideal generates,
on which `z ⊗ 1` vanishes because the augmentation ideal dies in `k`. -/
public lemma isPushout_realization :
    Algebra.IsPushout (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' k P := by
  let g : E.B' ⊗[TrivSqZeroExt k V] k →ₐ[E.B'] P :=
    Algebra.TensorProduct.lift (Algebra.ofId E.B' P)
      (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom (TrivSqZeroExt k V) k P) fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _
  have hg1 : ∀ c : k, g ((1 : E.B') ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] c) = algebraMap k P c := fun c ↦ by
    change Algebra.TensorProduct.lift _ _ _ _ = _
    rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.lift_tmul, map_one, one_mul]
    rfl
  have hgt : ∀ z : E.B', g (z ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] (1 : k)) = toRed E z := fun z ↦ by
    change Algebra.TensorProduct.lift _ _ _ _ = _
    rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.lift_tmul, map_one, mul_one]
    exact hred z
  refine ⟨IsBaseChange.of_equiv (LinearEquiv.ofBijective g.toLinearMap ⟨?_, ?_⟩) hg1⟩
  · intro x y hxy
    obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := exists_tmul_one E x
    obtain ⟨z', rfl⟩ := exists_tmul_one E y
    have h0 : toRed E (z - z') = 0 := by
      rw [map_sub, sub_eq_zero]
      exact (hgt z).symm.trans (hxy.trans (hgt z'))
    have h := map_eq_zero_of_mem_kerIdeal_smul
      ((TensorProduct.mk (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' k).flip 1) (fun a ha b ↦ by
        have hafst : (a : TrivSqZeroExt k V).fst = 0 := by
          rw [(mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V a).1 ha, fst_inr]
        rw [LinearMap.flip_apply, TensorProduct.mk_apply, TensorProduct.smul_tmul]
        change b ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] ((a : TrivSqZeroExt k V).fst * (1 : k)) = 0
        rw [hafst, zero_mul, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]) (kerCondition_toRed E hstr _ h0)
    rw [LinearMap.flip_apply, TensorProduct.mk_apply, TensorProduct.sub_tmul, sub_eq_zero] at h
    exact h
  · intro p
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := toRed_surjective E p
    exact ⟨z ⊗ₜ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] (1 : k), (hgt z).trans hz⟩

end Pushout

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
include hstr in
/-- **The cartesian square of the realized deformation, in `CommRingCat`.** This is
`Deformation.Examples.isPushout_realization` in the form the morphisms of the category of flat
algebras of Stacks 0DY1 are stated in, with the augmentation and the reduction given as bare
ring maps: an object of that category presents them through its own structure, so they are only
*extensionally* the first projection and the reduction of `E`. -/
public lemma isPushout_commRingCat_realization (aug : TrivSqZeroExt k V →+* k)
    (haug : ∀ a, aug a = a.fst) (red : E.B' →+* P) (hred : ∀ z, red z = toRed E z) :
    IsPushout (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'))
      (CommRingCat.ofHom aug) (CommRingCat.ofHom red)
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k P)) := by
  let : Algebra E.B' P := red.toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' P :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun a ↦ by
      change algebraMap k P a.fst = red (algebraMap (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' a)
      rw [hred, isFirstOrderReduction_toRed E hstr a]
  have : Module.Flat (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' := flat_realization E hstr
  have hpo := isPushout_realization E hstr hred
  have haugeq : (CommRingCat.ofHom aug : CommRingCat.of (TrivSqZeroExt k V) ⟶ CommRingCat.of k)
      = CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (TrivSqZeroExt k V) k) := by
    ext a
    exact haug a
  rw [haugeq]
  exact CommRingCat.isPushout_iff_isPushout.mpr hpo

end Realized

/-! ### The class of the extension determined by the realized deformation

The reduction a deformation-category datum supplies is a map of `k`-algebras for a `k`-algebra
structure on the middle ring of `E` which is *transported* from the base of the deformation, so
it is only propositionally the structure `E` carries. The statements below are therefore
parametric in that structure: the `k`-algebra structure on `E.B'` is a section variable, and the
hypothesis `hstr` pins its structural map down through
`Deformation.Examples.realizationHom`, which is enough to compare the two. -/

section RealizedBase

variable [Algebra (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] [Algebra k E.B']
  [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B']
  (hstr : ∀ a : TrivSqZeroExt k V,
    algebraMap (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B' a = realizationHom E a)

include hstr

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'] in
/-- The kernel condition for any reduction agreeing with the one of `E`. The reduction a
deformation-category datum supplies is only *extensionally* the reduction of `E`, so the
hypotheses of `Deformation.Examples.firstOrderExtension` are needed in this form. -/
public lemma kerCondition_of_eq_toRed (π : E.B' →ₐ[k] P) (hπeq : ∀ z, π z = toRed E z)
    (x : E.B') (hx : π x = 0) :
    x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B') :=
  kerCondition_toRed E hstr x ((hπeq x).symm.trans hx)

/-- **The ambient structural map of `E.B'` over `k` is the realizing structural map on `inl`.**
Through the tower `k → k ⊕ V → E.B'` the structural map of the ambient `k`-algebra structure is
`hstr` evaluated at `inl c`; composed with
`Deformation.Examples.realizationHom_inl` this identifies it with the structural map of the
`k`-algebra structure `E` itself carries. -/
public lemma algebraMap_eq_realizationHom_inl (c : k) :
    algebraMap k E.B' c = realizationHom E (inl c) := by
  rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B', algebraMap_eq_inl, hstr]

/-- The canonical map of the realized deformation, for any reduction agreeing with the one of
`E`, is the identification of the kernel `E` started from. -/
public lemma firstOrderConormalHom_eq_kerIncl' (π : E.B' →ₐ[k] P)
    (hπ : Function.Surjective π) (hπeq : ∀ z, π z = toRed E z) (x : P ⊗[k] V) :
    firstOrderConormalHom (V := V) π hπ x = kerIncl E x := by
  induction x with
  | tmul p v =>
      obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := hπ p
      rw [firstOrderConormalHom_tmul π hπ (kerCondition_of_eq_toRed E hstr π hπeq) p v q hq,
        inr_smul_eq_kerIncl E hstr, ← hπeq q, hq]
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy]

/-- **The square-zero extension determined by the realized deformation is `E` itself**, for any
reduction agreeing with the one of `E`. The middle ring and the reduction are those of `E` and
the identifications of the kernel agree by
`Deformation.Examples.firstOrderConormalHom_eq_kerIncl'`.

The comparison of the two `k`-algebra structures on that ring is the identity of the ring: both
structural maps send `c` to the value of `Deformation.Examples.realizationHom` at `inl c`, the
ambient one through the tower `k → k ⊕ V → E.B'` and `hstr`, the structure of `E` by
`Deformation.Examples.realizationHom_inl`. -/
public def isoRealizationOfEq (π : E.B' →ₐ[k] P) (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π)
    (hker : ∀ x : E.B', π x = 0 → x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'))
    (hπeq : ∀ z, π z = toRed E z) :
    letI := flat_realization E hstr
    SquareZeroExtensionProblem.CompatibleExtension.Iso
      (firstOrderExtension (V := V) π hπ hπa hker) E :=
  letI := flat_realization E hstr
  { toAlgEquiv := AlgEquiv.ofRingEquiv (f := RingEquiv.refl E.B') fun c ↦
      (algebraMap_eq_realizationHom_inl E hstr c).trans (realizationHom_inl E c)
    toB_comm := AlgHom.ext fun z ↦ (hπeq z).symm
    kernelEquiv_comm := fun n ↦
      (kernelInclusion_firstOrderExtension (V := V) π hπ hπa hker n).trans
        (firstOrderConormalHom_eq_kerIncl' E hstr π hπ hπeq n) }

/-- **The class of the extension determined by the realized deformation is the class of `E`.**
This is the surjectivity half of the tangent-space clause of Stacks 0DY3 in the form a
deformation-category datum delivers it: the reduction such a datum supplies is only
extensionally the reduction of `E`, and its `k`-algebra structure only propositionally the one
of `E`. -/
public lemma extClass_firstOrderExtension_eq (π : E.B' →ₐ[k] P) (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π)
    (hker : ∀ x : E.B', π x = 0 → x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) E.B'))
    (hπeq : ∀ z, π z = toRed E z) :
    letI := flat_realization E hstr
    extClass (firstOrderExtension (V := V) π hπ hπa hker) = extClass E :=
  letI := flat_realization E hstr
  congrArg (squareZeroAlgebraExtensionClassesEquivExtOne k P (P ⊗[k] V))
    (Quotient.sound ⟨isoRealizationOfEq E hstr π hπ hπa hker hπeq⟩)

end RealizedBase

/-! ### The extension determined by the realized deformation -/

/-- **The square-zero extension determined by the realized deformation is `E` itself.** The
underlying ring and the reduction are those of `E` on the nose, and the identification of the
kernel agrees by `Deformation.Examples.firstOrderConormalHom_eq_kerIncl`. -/
public def isoRealization :
    letI := realizationAlgebra E
    letI := realizationIsScalarTower E
    letI := flat_realization E fun _ ↦ rfl
    SquareZeroExtensionProblem.CompatibleExtension.Iso
      (firstOrderExtension (V := V) (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E)
        (isFirstOrderReduction_toRed E fun _ ↦ rfl)
        (kerCondition_toRed E fun _ ↦ rfl)) E :=
  letI := realizationAlgebra E
  letI := realizationIsScalarTower E
  letI := flat_realization E fun _ ↦ rfl
  { toAlgEquiv := AlgEquiv.refl
    toB_comm := rfl
    kernelEquiv_comm := fun n ↦
      (kernelInclusion_firstOrderExtension (V := V) (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E)
        (isFirstOrderReduction_toRed E fun _ ↦ rfl)
        (kerCondition_toRed E fun _ ↦ rfl) n).trans
        (firstOrderConormalHom_eq_kerIncl E (fun _ ↦ rfl) n) }

/-- **Every class in `Ext¹_P(NL_{P/k}, P ⊗[k] V)` is the class of a first-order flat
deformation of `P` over `k ⊕ V`.** This is the surjectivity half of the tangent-space clause of
Stacks 0DY3: the class of the extension determined by the deformation
`Deformation.Examples.realizationAlgebra` realizing `E` is the class of `E`, and by Stacks 0GPT
every class is the class of some `E`. -/
public lemma extClass_firstOrderExtension_realization :
    letI := realizationAlgebra E
    letI := realizationIsScalarTower E
    letI := flat_realization E fun _ ↦ rfl
    extClass (firstOrderExtension (V := V) (toRed E) (toRed_surjective E)
        (isFirstOrderReduction_toRed E fun _ ↦ rfl)
        (kerCondition_toRed E fun _ ↦ rfl)) = extClass E :=
  letI := realizationAlgebra E
  letI := realizationIsScalarTower E
  letI := flat_realization E fun _ ↦ rfl
  congrArg (squareZeroAlgebraExtensionClassesEquivExtOne k P (P ⊗[k] V))
    (Quotient.sound ⟨isoRealization E⟩)

end Realization

end Deformation.Examples

